 "notes": [
  "Built with MPFB 2.0.18 (MakeHuman) inside Blender 5.0.1: male, age 25 (age macro 0.5), muscle 0.78, weight 0.54, proportions 0.9, race mix caucasian 0.5 / asian 0.3 / african 0.2 plus face/torso detail targets; height macro solved numerically for 1.78 m. Skin = MakeHuman young_caucasian_male texture graded to medium-brown.",
  "Rig = MPFB 'game_engine' (53 deform bones incl. fingers). MPFB names its root bone 'Root'; it was renamed to 'root'.",
  "Body was decimated from 26.8k to ~19.5k triangles with per-region budgets (head 6.9k, hands 3.9k, feet 1k), then split by dominant bone weight into 8 parts. Seam vertices are duplicated with identical skin weights and the unsplit body's normals are stored as custom normals, so the parts are watertight and seamless when all are shown.",
  "Body_Head uses its own 453x1024 crop of the 2048 source skin atlas (material M_Skin_Head) for a sharper face; the rest of the body uses M_Skin_Body (1024). A dark short-hair tone is painted on the scalp under the hair cards so the head still reads as short dark hair where Hair_Default is hidden.",
  "Hair_Default is hidden in DESERT FOX (cap) and SHADOW OPS (helmet) because the hair cards clip through the cap/helmet crown; the painted scalp shows as a short buzz under them.",
  "Body_Feet is hidden in every bundle (all have footwear; footwear soles were lifted 3-26 mm so they sit on Z=0). Bundle 'hide' lists only contain parts fully enclosed by that outfit (ray-cast coverage + MakeHuman delete groups + visual checks), so applying them never opens a hole; parts not listed may be partially covered and stay visible.",
  "Clothes: ROOKIE = elvs crude t-shirt (flat white), toigo wool pants cut 7.5 cm above the knee into charcoal shorts (no male shorts in the packs; MakeHuman jeans shorts are hot-pants), shoes05 white sneakers. DESERT FOX = namuhekam polo (khaki), cortu cargo pants (olive, subdivided once), toigo ankle boots (brown), toigo baseball cap re-coloured plain tan (original print removed). NEON STRIKER = male_casualsuit05 jacket+shirt+jeans re-coloured black jacket / cyan striped shirt / dark jeans, shoes05 with cyan accents, medical mouth mask re-coloured black with cyan edges and tightened to the face. SHADOW OPS = fisherman sweater (black), cargo pants (black), shoes03 boots (black), M1 helmet (dense camouflage-net shell removed, shell deepened, matte black), toigo short gloves (black). ROYAL GOLD = galactic warrior uniform re-coloured white with gold panels, shoes01 re-coloured gold (metallic 0.6).",
  "Layered garments were de-intersected in the rest pose (outer layers pushed outside inner layers / skin). Minor clipping can still appear at extreme joint angles (e.g. death pose hips, deep crouch).",
  "All animations are 30 fps, baked FK (rotation keys on all bones, location on pelvis; root never moves). Locomotion is in place: run cycles 0.7 s / stride 1.4 m (2.0 m/s at 1x), crouch_fwd 1.0 s / 1.0 m. death translates the pelvis ~0.5 m backwards while falling (root stays at origin). Looping clips have last frame == first frame.",
  "Gameplay clips (idle, run_*, crouch_*, jump) keep both wrists at a fixed grip relative to spine_03 (rifle follows the chest). The gun is not in the file; previews show a placeholder rifle parented to hand_r.",
  "glTF/Godot axes: Blender (x, y, z) -> glTF (x, z, -y). The character faces +Z in Godot; *_godot rifle positions are already converted.",
  "All outfit materials are double-sided (glTF doubleSided) because garments contain legitimate inner faces (collars, hems, liners, cap brim); body/eyes are single-sided.",
  "Known minor artifact: the skin-tight ROOKIE t-shirt can show a few millimetre-sized specks of skin near its hem in some poses (garments were de-intersected against skin and inner layers in both directions, and tight tops use skin-transferred weights, but the tee is very close to the body).",
  "No twist bones in the game_engine rig: forearm roll is carried by the hand bone, so extreme wrist twists can pinch slightly at the wrist."
 ],
